# Wave W17-R (Route 125): ebb rock — ice-fringed cave-isle rock standing in the lane’s water: a cool grey isle rock whose upper faces carry a fringe of pale ice where Ebbtide Cave’s cold breath spills onto its own island — the glinting ice falls of the design drawn at the rock’s crown, foam collar at its base, the sea baked in around it (design: the cave isle’s mouths fringed with ice falls glinting in the shadow). Route 125’s own rock — the fleet’s only frost-fringed rock: split from Route 126’s warm massive crater rock by temperature and finish (ice at the crown vs plain warm joints).
